# Mohamed Ali — Professional Portfolio Website

Build a production-ready, multi-page portfolio website for a Robotics & Mechatronics Engineer, featuring dark/light mode, dynamic project pages, 3D CAD viewer, lecture gallery, and a documentation-style navigation system.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Tech Stack Choice:** I'm proposing **Next.js 15 (App Router) + Tailwind CSS v4 + Framer Motion + Three.js**. This gives us:
> - Static Site Generation (SSG) for free hosting on Vercel/Netlify
> - File-based routing for clean URLs (`/projects/robotic-arm`, `/lectures`)
> - React Server Components for fast initial loads
> - Easy JSON-driven dynamic pages
>
> **Alternative:** If you prefer a simpler setup (no Node.js build step for hosting), we could use Vite + React. But Next.js is ideal for Vercel deployment.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Hosting Recommendation:** **Vercel** (free tier) is the best option for this Next.js site:
> - Zero-config deployment — just connect your GitHub repo
> - Free custom domain support
> - Automatic HTTPS, CDN, and preview deployments
> - Perfect for static/SSG Next.js sites
>
> **Alternatives:** Netlify (also free), GitHub Pages (needs `next export`), Cloudflare Pages.

> [!WARNING]
> **3D CAD Viewer:** The `.stl`/`.glb` viewer using Three.js will add ~150KB to the bundle. It will only load on project pages that actually include 3D models (code-split). You'll need to convert your SolidWorks files to `.glb` or `.stl` format for the viewer — I'll document how.

